      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_4",
        on: "start",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Grimnir",
            text: _("This passage leads very close to the trolls’ main lair; you can hear them tromping back and forth just past the eastern wall. All that separates us from the trolls is a thin wall of stone. I’ve had me boys mine the end of the tunnel with explosives; when you move a unit adjacent to the final wall, I’ll blow the charges and open the way. The troll leader should only be lightly defended; he’s sent most of his best warriors to the front. You’ll know the head troll when you see him — he’s big, gray and extra ugly."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Nym",
            text: _("I thought that’s what all the trolls looked like. I suppose we’ll just try to find the one that shouts the loudest."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Zhul",
            text: _("So you dug these tunnels all by yourselves?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Grimnir",
            text: _("Long ago, before the damned trolls invaded, we spent our days digging tunnels all through these mountains. Oh the ore and precious stones we mined! The mines were filled with the joyful sound of dwarven hammer and dwarven song and our jeweled halls glowed as brightly as the sun. Human and elf princes would pay us royally for the craftsmanship of our forges. But now the tunnels are silent and we spend our days hunting those accursed trolls. But there’s no point dwelling on the past. There’s more work to be done! Still, we have our honor and I promise you, do this for us and you will be rewarded handsomely."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Kaleh",
            text: _("It shall be done."),
          },
        ],
      },
